==Battleground==
*1 [[Sunfish Jones]] spawns as the boss after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*20 [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 10.67 seconds<sup>320f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*20 [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 11.33 seconds<sup>340f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*20 [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 12 seconds<sup>360f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*5 [[Calamary|Calamaries]] spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Boraphim]] spawns after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Trolly Blogger]]s spawn after 200 seconds<sup>6,000f</sup>, delay 20~30 seconds<sup>600f~900f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The usual [[Juliet Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Princess Juliet Cat]] + [[Cat Toaster (Super Rare Cat)|Cat Projector]] stacking strategy is an option, just riskier. If you're going to do it, make sure to lure Boraphim as close as possible so your stack doesn't immediately charge into Sunfish Jones's range; and keep an eye on your wallet! Once afflicted with statuses, try to rush down Boraphim with high-damage units such as [[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Delivery Cat]], [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]. To deal with the backline Calamaries, snipe them with [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]] and [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Crimson Mina]].

Another addition that could be added is [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]], as if it gets knocked back by the Trolly Bloggers, it will instantly attack again, making it an efficient way to get a lot of money quickly.

There is an alternative strategy that doesn't require Freezing nor Slowing Boraphim. In your first row you will need [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]] and [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]] or some other "Research" Effect Up [[Cat Combo]] to make [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] spammable. You may also want [[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Prof. Cat Jobs]], as well as Crazed Sexy Legs Cat. On row 2 you need [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|dual]] [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Erasers]], Ramen Cat, [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge Cat]] and Awakened Bahamut Cat. Start off by stalling with Crazed Sexy Legs to get your [[Worker Cat]] to level 3/4 until Boraphim comes out. Then, spam all but your non-Combo cats. The main damage will be done by Bahamut. Stall and cycle Awakened Bahamuts until Boraphim dies, then the rest should be easy.

Most [[:Category:Anti-Angel Cats|anti-Angel]] [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rares]] you have, particularly those that can slow or freeze, as well as any long-range units like [[Radiant Aphrodite (Uber Rare Cat)|Megaphrodite]] or [[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Super Galaxy Cosmo]] will help.

==Trivia==
*There is a typo in the name of this stage. It is named "Irresistable Henhouse" when it should be "Irresist𝘪ble Henhouse".
*Since it's found in [[Mouseyland]], Irresistable Henhouse's Japanese name, Yūneku no Chikin Rūmu (誘惑のチキンルーム, "Irresistible Chicken Room"), is most likely a reference to Disneyland's [[wikipedia:Walt Disney's Enchanted Tiki Room|Enchanted Tiki Room]], which is called Miwaku no Chiki Rūmu (魅惑のチキルーム) in Japanese.
**It may also be a reference to [https://coasterpedia.net/wiki/Chicken_exit chicken exits], where guests can exit a ride's queue line should they "chicken out" of going on the ride.

